# The forest snail's body (#329, D101, D106): the `dead` frame of snail.grid, pixel for pixel, in a decor-tier
# palette (D76): a dim colour with a contour in its own hue, no ink 0b0814, no moon rim, so the empty shell never reads
# as a live snail. Keep it in step with snail.grid.
# Forest recolour (#236, D108, 2026-11-20): hand-set tone roles (hollow m, contour k, shade s, rim o, shell S, whorl t, lip c)
# on one dark umber (OKLab L 0.143 to 0.253, chroma 0.055, hue 50): an emptied, dried shell. Its spots are forest-1's near-black
# ground and the blue night forest behind the ledges; the warm hue keeps it off that blue (D108 band 0.08..0.20); no ink.
size 24 16
color k 1e0600
color o 270d00
color s 250900
color S 2a0e00
color t 301302
color c 341b0c
color m 170400
frame body
